  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2008-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since the mean of the first \\(n\\) terms is \\(n,\\) their sum is \\(n^2.\\)\n\nThe \\(n\\)th term is \\(n^2-(n-1)^2=2n-1,\\) so the \\(2008\\)th term is \\(2\\cdot 2008-1=4015.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms is \\(n\\cdot n=n^2\\)",
        "The \\(n\\)th term is \\(n^2-(n-1)^2\\)"
      ],
